dialect protocol
protocol stdio.pdf.1.7.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.pdf.1.7.op
start record

# P2-FG3: REAL binary op frame (`format u8 | tag u8 | variant payload`), matching this file's own
# `header fixed 2` + `chain payload bytes` shape -- upgraded from F6's `print_op().into_bytes()`
# text-as-binary shortcut (../../🦀️component.rs's old `OpBinary::encode_op`, per the mandatory
# FG1/FG2 binary-frame lesson: every standard's `OpBinary` gets a REAL frame, not just a
# fixed-header-then-text-bytes cosmetic wrapper -- the payload past `format`/`tag` is genuine
# LEB128-varint/length-prefixed binary, `enc_pdf_object_bin`/`enc_pdf_snapshot_bin`/... in that
# same file's `OpBinaryCodec` region, reusing the diff facet's own `pub(crate)` binary primitives
# the same way its text `OpText` reuses the diff facet's text primitives). `tag` is the
# `PdfMutation` variant ordinal, in the SAME 0-14 order `print_pdf_mutation`'s own keyword match
# uses (`NoMutation`=0, `SetSnapshot`=1, `InsertPage`=2, `RemovePage`=3, `SetPageMediaBox`=4,
# `SetPageCropBox`=5, `AppendPageContent`=6, `SetInfo`=7, `InsertObject`=8, `RemoveObject`=9,
# `SetObjectValue`=10, `SetDictEntry`=11, `RemoveDictEntry`=12, `SetTrailerEntry`=13,
# `RemoveTrailerEntry`=14).
#
# The recursive/data-carrying payload (`PdfObject`, `PdfSnapshot`, `PdfPathSegment` chains) is NOT
# re-modeled field-by-field here -- `Prim::Ref` (the only construct that could describe it)
# unconditionally errors during `walk_protocol` (`protocol-prim-ref-recursion`, hit by every
# stdio pilot's own recursive mutation/diff payload). This is the same honest-boundary treatment
# every other upgraded pilot's opaque payload tail uses: the Rust `encode_op`/`decode_op` side is
# genuinely, fully recursive binary and round-trip tested independently (`op_text_binary_
# roundtrip_law`).
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8
chain payload bytes
